Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:55:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/24] prompt-audit K4: audit.md points at where the demotion
 rule lives now

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 commands/claudemd-audit.md | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/commands/claudemd-audit.md b/commands/claudemd-audit.md
index 9738fba..c5b90a1 100644
--- a/commands/claudemd-audit.md
+++ b/commands/claudemd-audit.md
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@ The JSON contains:
 
 For `denyByProjectClass`: report each hook's deny split as `<external> external / <self> self / <unknown> unknown` and **lead with the `external` count as the real downstream-interception signal** — do NOT present the raw deny total as the enforcement value (most of it is the plugin's own dogfood; see the 498/516 banned-vocab finding).
 
-Format per-hook sections, the bySection heatmap (sorted by total desc), and call out any `byBypass` token with ≥3 occurrences as "review candidate" (where `suppressed` is recorded, count `suppressed.yes`, not `total`) per §0.1 demotion principle, and for each such token print its top `bySubject` entries — the subject is what makes the candidate actionable ("`vars:SCRATCH` ×9" is a gate mis-shaped for sandbox cleanup; nine different subjects is nine one-offs and no rule change). If a token's subjects are all `(no subject)`, say so rather than inferring — those rows predate the field. Surface `uniqueInvocations.<hook>.duplicate_rows_real > 0` for any PreToolUse/PostToolUse hook as a candidate registration/lib bug — EXCEPT for multi-emit hooks (pre-bash-safety logs one row per matched pattern in a compound command), where a residual `_real` can come from one command repeating the SAME pattern (`rm -rf $D; …; rm -rf $D`); telemetry can't distinguish that from a double-registration, so confirm against the source command before reporting a bug. **Do NOT report bare `duplicate_rows`** — that number includes legacy collision noise (`duplicate_rows_legacy`) which is expected for pre-v0.9.34 rows and Stop/SessionStart-class hooks. Always read the `_real` / `_legacy` split, never the bare sum.
+Format per-hook sections, the bySection heatmap (sorted by total desc), and call out any `byBypass` token with ≥3 occurrences as "review candidate" (where `suppressed` is recorded, count `suppressed.yes`, not `total`) per the OPERATOR.md §13.1 demotion review, and for each such token print its top `bySubject` entries — the subject is what makes the candidate actionable ("`vars:SCRATCH` ×9" is a gate mis-shaped for sandbox cleanup; nine different subjects is nine one-offs and no rule change). If a token's subjects are all `(no subject)`, say so rather than inferring — those rows predate the field. Surface `uniqueInvocations.<hook>.duplicate_rows_real > 0` for any PreToolUse/PostToolUse hook as a candidate registration/lib bug — EXCEPT for multi-emit hooks (pre-bash-safety logs one row per matched pattern in a compound command), where a residual `_real` can come from one command repeating the SAME pattern (`rm -rf $D; …; rm -rf $D`); telemetry can't distinguish that from a double-registration, so confirm against the source command before reporting a bug. **Do NOT report bare `duplicate_rows`** — that number includes legacy collision noise (`duplicate_rows_legacy`) which is expected for pre-v0.9.34 rows and Stop/SessionStart-class hooks. Always read the `_real` / `_legacy` split, never the bare sum.
 
 For `bySection['(unset-historical)']`: note as pre-v0.7.0 legacy data — will age out of the window naturally; do NOT include in the heatmap leader.
 
